This solution uses a breadth-first search (BFS) approach to perform topological sorting on a directed graph. It first identifies nodes with no incoming edges (which are the starting points of the sorting process) and then iteratively adds these nodes to the result list until all nodes have been processed. If the final number of processed nodes does not match the total number of nodes, the graph contains cycles, and a `ValueError` is raised.
